{{Quote|They can outrun me, but they can't outrun XLR8!|Ben.<ref>''[[A Jolt From the Past]]''</ref>}}
XLR8 is a speedster with lightning-quick reflexes and the ability to reach speeds in excess of 500 miles per hour.{{Refn|group = Bandai|name = Bandai}} He can accelerate so quickly that time appears to completely stop to him, allowing him to change the positions of things around him mid-motion, while only being able to be seen by a camera with a very high shutter speed.<ref name="The Unnaturals">''[[The Unnaturals]]''</ref> His speed power comes from manipulating friction,{{Refn|According to [[Duncan Rouleau]], XLR8 is "completely frictionless".{{Refn|[[:File:XLR8 Is Frictionless.png]]|group = DR}} However, this is contradicted by the many times XLR8 has been shown skidding to a stop, tumbling across the ground, etc.{{Refn|[[Ben 10 Planet:Policies/Canon Hierarchy|Canon Hierarchy]]|group = BTP}} Correlating with Duncan, a cereal card states that XLR8 can instead manipulate his friction.{{Refn|[[:File:XLR8 Cereal Card.png]]|group = CN}}|group = note}} so he can also run up sheer walls<ref name="TGE">''[[The Galactic Enforcers]]''</ref> and across non-solid grounds like water.<ref name="The Krakken">''[[The Krakken]]''</ref><ref name="BwaV">''[[Back With a Vengeance]]''</ref> Additionally, XLR8's tremendous speed and aerodynamic body makes him resistant to strong winds, such as the suction force of [[Dr. Viktor]]'s portal.<ref name="TR />

XLR8 has the potential to become even faster with age, seen when [[Ben 10,000 (Original)|Ben 10,000]] as XLR8 managed to outrun [[Ken Tennyson (Original)|Ken]] as XLR8 in a race, even when Ken had a head start.<ref name="Ken 10" /> XLR8 was also capable of travelling globally in just a few seconds when used by Ben 10,000.{{Refn|[[:File:Ben10K XLR8 Patrol.png]]|group = pop-up}}<ref name="Ben 10,000">''[[Ben 10,000 (Episode)|Ben 10,000]]''</ref> This also boosts his strength, shown when his XLR8 was able to greatly damage [[Exo-Skull|Exo-Skull]] with speed-enhanced physical attacks.<ref name="Ben 10,000" />

Compared to his fellow speedster alien [[Fasttrack]], XLR8 seems to have more control over his speed; he can immediately end a run by stopping in place, while Fasttrack can have trouble stopping if he runs too fast.<ref>''[[The Eggman Cometh]]''</ref> Furthermore, he is confirmed to be faster than [[Aerophibian (Classic)|Aerophibians]] on the ground.{{Refn|[[:File:XLR8 and Jetray Speed.PNG]]|group = DM}}

Even without his incredible running speed, XLR8 is capable of thinking, acting, and reacting at superhuman speed. His sharp reflexes allow him to dodge attacks with little to no effort,<ref name="TR">''[[The Return]]''</ref><ref name="B10VtN10P1">''[[Ben 10 vs. Negative 10: Part 1]]''</ref> and change direction very easily while running. He is able to type on keyboards or keypads at high speeds. When using this skill to bypass a multiple-digit code, he can think of and input every single possible combination instead of guessing, as he did when trying to remove [[SevenSeven (Dimension 23)|SevenSeven 23]]'s bomb from [[Ben 23]]'s arm.<ref name="Store 23">''[[Store 23]]''</ref>

XLR8 is capable of creating vortexes by generating a centripetal vacuum powerful enough to lift a [[To'kustar (Classic)|To'kustar]],<ref>''[[The Frogs of War: Part 2]]''</ref> either by running in a circular pattern or spinning at supersonic speeds.<ref name="MW">''[[Monster Weather]]''</ref><ref name="MC">''[[Merry Christmas]]''</ref> He can also combine this with water running to create water vortexes by running in front of or around his enemies.<ref name="The Krakken" /><ref name="AND" /> He can even combine this with fire, as demonstrated by [[Helen Wheels|Helen]].<ref name="AaB">''[[Above and Beyond]]''</ref>

XLR8 can deliver attacks in rapid succession, such as excessively kicking,<ref name="The Krakken" /> or stabbing with his scissor-like claws.<ref>''[[Camp Fear]]''</ref>

XLR8 has great amounts of strength, as he was able to lift multiple people without slowing down while running on water.<ref name="The Krakken" /> His strength shines the most with striking, as he was able to punch [[Rojo]] harder the shell of a military tank could.<ref name="The Alliance"/>

XLR8 is durable enough to withstand being thrown against a wall,<ref name="MHR">''[[Many Happy Returns]]''</ref> and can adversely survive coming to a dead stop at full speed.<ref>''[[Secrets]]''</ref>

XLR8 is capable of jumping exceptionally high, and incredibly far when his jump height is mixed with his speed.<ref name="MW" />

XLR8's tail is prehensile, and can hold objects if his hands are full, as XLR8 held a [[Null Void Containment Egg]] with it when he was about to trap [[Devlin Levin|Devlin]].<ref name="Ken 10">''[[Ken 10]]''</ref> This feat was first demonstrated when [[Kevin 11]] used his tail to carefully pick up a tray of slop and shove it in [[Technorg|Technorg's]] face when he wasn't looking.<ref>''[[Grudge Match]]''</ref>

XLR8 has a natural retractable visor hidden under his helmet. This visor helps to guard his face when running at high speeds for long periods of time.

