==Etymology==
XLR8's name is a [[wikipedia:gramogram|gramogram]] of the word "accelerate", referencing his enhanced speed.

==Trivia==
*XLR8's appearance in ''[[The Krakken]]'' is the first mistransformation in the '''[[Ben 10 (2005 TV Series)|Original Series]]''' and the [[Ben 10 (Franchise)|franchise]] as a whole.
*A common misconception about XLR8 is that the balls on his feet are referred to as wheels. This even occurs within the [[Ben 10 (2016 TV Series)|Reboot]].<ref>''[[High Stress Express]]'' </ref>
*A buzzing-like sound effect can be heard whenever XLR8 speaks.
*XLR8 and [[NRG]] are the only aliens whose names are gramograms.
*XLR8 was the winner of a [[Cartoon Network]] '''Ben 10''' alien poll that only had the first 12 aliens.
*XLR8's visor is made up of his skin and part of his skull.{{Refn|[[:File:Kineceleran Visor Details.png]]|group = DR}}
*Originally, XLR8 was the only [[Kineceleran (Classic)|Kineceleran]] on [[Earth (Classic)|Earth]] because the slow rotation of said planet made other Kinecelerans sick after a few days.{{Refn|[[:File:Kineceleran Sick.png]]|group = pop-up}}<ref name="Ben 10,000" /> This was retconned in '''[[Ben 10: Omniverse (TV Series)|Omniverse]]''', as several Kinecelerans reside in [[Undertown]].<ref>''[[The More Things Change: Part 2]]''</ref>
*XLR8's speed trail in '''[[Ben 10: Omniverse (TV Series)|Omniverse]]''' is a reused asset from an earlier [[Derrick J. Wyatt]] project, ''[https://tfwiki.net/wiki/Transformers_Animated_(cartoon) Transformers Animated]'', as the trail of the speedster character [https://tfwiki.net/wiki/Blurr_(Animated) Blurr].
*XLR8's [[Ben 10 (2005 TV Series)/Early Development#XLR8|pre-production design]] was drawn by Steven E. Gordon. He had the same name, powers, and skin color, but was much more humanoid before the crew switched from superheroes to aliens. [[Dave Johnson]] designed him but noted that like [[Ripjaws (Classic)|Ripjaws]] and [[Wildmutt]], it was hard for outsourced animators to draw him, particularly his hands.{{Refn|https://archive.is/zNL9t|group = DJ}}
*XLR8 was originally intended to be used in ''[[Couples Retreat]]''.{{Refn|[https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/ben10/images/e/ef/Couples_Retreat_Draft-1.pdf ''Couples Retreat'' Script First Draft]|group = script|name = script}} In the final version, his role was taken by [[Fasttrack]].
*XLR8's name was used in a {{w|XLR8|Pop dance group}} in the {{W|Philippines}}, as well as on a CD about different technical institutes by the {{w|Universal Technical Institute}}.
*[[Matt Wayne]] speculated that XLR8 is physically weaker than [[Fasttrack]], stating that "Fasttrack can probably lift more".{{Refn|[[:File:Fasttrack Physically Stronger Than XLR8.PNG]]|group = MW}}

